.TH PRINTENV 1 "2026-11-15"
.SH NAME
printenv \- Display the values of the specified environment VARIABLE(s), or (with no VARIABLE) display name and value pairs for them all.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBprintenv\fR [OPTION]... [VARIABLE]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Display the values of the specified environment VARIABLE(s), or (with no VARIABLE) display name and value pairs for them all.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-0\fR, \fB\-\-null\fR
end each output line with 0 byte rather than newline
.TP
\fB\-\-quoting\-style\fR
Set quoting style

\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
literal
.IP \(bu 2
locale
.IP \(bu 2
shell
.IP \(bu 2
shell\-escape
.IP \(bu 2
shell\-always
.IP \(bu 2
shell\-escape\-always
.IP \(bu 2
clocale
.IP \(bu 2
c
.IP \(bu 2
c\-maybe
.IP \(bu 2
escape
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIvariables\fR]

.SH VERSION
